1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,160
Matcha, if your stomach burns every time you drink it, there's a reason.

2
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:07,360
Matcha isn't steeped and strained like regular tea.

3
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:15,760
You drink the whole leaf, ground into powder, so far more catechins and caffeine end up in your cup than in a cup of brewed green tea.

4
00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:23,200
Three things explain why matcha can leave your stomach burning: tannins, caffeine, and how people are drinking it lately.

5
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:24,880
First, tannins.

6
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:35,360
Matcha's tannins stimulate acid production in the stomach lining directly, and a full dose of whole-leaf powder delivers a much stronger hit than steeped tea ever could.

7
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:37,120
Second, caffeine.

8
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:44,160
Matcha has a mild, gentle reputation, but a well-made cup carries about as much caffeine as coffee.

9
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:48,640
On an empty stomach, that caffeine pushes acid production even higher.

10
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:50,800
Third, the trend itself.

11
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:57,920
Many people now treat a matcha latte as their entire breakfast, skipping food and drinking it straight on an empty stomach.

12
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:04,800
That habit lets both the tannins and the caffeine hit unbuffered, right when your stomach is most sensitive.

13
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:10,320
Drink matcha after a meal, not instead of one, and keep it to two cups a day.

14
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:15,360
Choose a lighter brew instead of a concentrated shot, and the burning stops.
